Licences of TORCS for RISC OS
=============================

The program !RunImage contains TORCS and the libraries below, all linked
into one file. The source code of TORCS, the RISC OS changes and the
scripts that build everything are in the riscos-torcs repository
(patches against Debian's torcs 1.3.7+dfsg source); the libraries'
sources are the tarballs named in its build/SHA256SUMS. GPL section 3:
the corresponding source is available from the same place as this zip.

TORCS 1.3.7 (Debian's torcs_1.3.7+dfsg source)     GNU GPL 2 or later:
    COPYING. Some files are under other licences; the game data (cars,
    tracks, robots' settings) too: TORCS-data (Debian's copyright file,
    which lists them).
plib 1.8.5 (sg, ssg, ssgAux, ul, js, sl)          GNU LGPL 2 or later,
    with Steve Baker's linking exception: plib-COPYING.
freealut 1.1.0                                     GNU LGPL 2:
    freealut-COPYING.
libpng 1.6.37                                      libpng licence:
    libpng-LICENSE.
libogg 1.3.5, libvorbis 1.3.7                      BSD licences:
    libogg-COPYING, libvorbis-COPYING.
riscos-mesa devkit 12f: Mesa (OSMesa), riscos-mesa's EGL, GLU,
    freeglut, SDL 2, OpenAL Soft, zlib, UnixLib (the C library) and
    the PThreadTicker module: riscos-mesa-devkit-LICENCES (and
    PThreadTicker-Licence in the application).

The LGPL libraries (plib, freealut, OpenAL Soft) are linked statically.
To relink TORCS with a changed version of one of them, build it from
the riscos-torcs repository (build/build-deps.sh, then
build/build-torcs.sh): every object file and script is there.
